(Plan 230 stage A2 — the backwards-compatibility case the whole design exists
for: TWO VERSIONS of one library in a single .so, both callable, resolving to
different code. This is version 0.1 of `flags`. It is linked with
flags_1_0.vox (version 1.0) by `vox flags_0_1.vox flags_1_0.vox --shared -o
libflags.so`; both define `hasflag`, and the mangling keeps them apart:
flags_0_1_hasflag vs flags_1_0_hasflag.

`hasflag` here returns n add 1, so hasflag(5) equals 6. The 1.0 build returns
n add 100 (equals 105). The driver calls both and checks each result, proving
the two versions are independently callable from one .so — the property most
likely to regress silently, so test.sh builds and runs it on every host.)

Library "flags" version "0.1".

To "hasflag" with a number called "n".
  Return n add 1.